% Logical Thinking in the Age of AI, slide 6 (continued): "Within the Medical
% Realm" - PROBLEM SOLVING: what would have to be true for a treatment to be
% the right one?
%
% Section 3.1 and Fig. 1 of Chen et al., https://arxiv.org/pdf/1610.08115,
% with two more sentences of the ACCF/AHA guideline:
%  - Combination of hydralazine & isosorbide dinitrate is recommended to
%    reduce morbidity & mortality for patients self-described as African
%    Americans with NYHA class III-IV HFrEF receiving optimal therapy with ACE
%    inhibitors & beta blockers, unless contraindicated.
%  - Combination of hydralazine & isosorbide dinitrate should not be used for
%    the treatment of HFrEF in patients who have no prior use of standard
%    neurohormonal antagonist therapy.
%
% "Suppose we have an African American patient who is suffering from NYHA
% class III HFrEF, but that is all we know about the patient." Is the
% combination recommended? Not a yes or a no, but a CONDITIONAL answer: yes,
% if the patient has received standard neurohormonal antagonist therapy - a
% precise description of the solution, including what is still to be checked.
% The template below is assumable (abducible): when nothing says whether it
% holds, the reasoner may assume it, and reports the assumption with the
% answer (scenario what_we_know). The paper's s(ASP) answer set (Fig. 1):
%   { accf stage(c), hf with reduced ef,
%     history(standard neurohormonal antagonist therapy), nyha class(3),
%     nyha class 3 to 4, race(african american),
%     recommendation(hydralazine and isosorbide dinitrate,class 1),
%     not contraindication(hydralazine and isosorbide dinitrate) }
%
% The rest of the guideline comes from heart_failure.le, included as a
% resource.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base heart_failure_what_if includes these resources:
    heart_failure.

the templates are:
    *a patient* identifies as African American; undefined.
    *a patient* has received standard neurohormonal antagonist therapy; assumable.

the knowledge base heart_failure_what_if includes:

% The paper, like the guideline's second sentence, reads "receiving optimal
% therapy with ACE inhibitors and beta blockers" as having received standard
% neurohormonal antagonist therapy.
a patient has an indication for hydralazine plus isosorbide dinitrate with class 1
    if the patient identifies as African American
    and the patient has heart failure with reduced ejection fraction
    and the NYHA class of the patient is a number N
    and N >= 3
    and the patient has received standard neurohormonal antagonist therapy.

a patient has a contraindication to hydralazine plus isosorbide dinitrate
    if the patient has heart failure with reduced ejection fraction
    and it is not the case that
        the patient has received standard neurohormonal antagonist therapy.

% All we know about Dan.
scenario what_we_know is:
    Dan identifies as African American.
    Dan is in stage C.
    the NYHA class of Dan is 3.
    the ejection fraction of Dan is 30.
    combination expects answers [
        "the guideline recommends hydralazine plus isosorbide dinitrate with class 1 for Dan"]
        and unknowns ["Dan has received standard neurohormonal antagonist therapy"].

% Once the record shows the therapy, the answer is unconditional.
scenario after_checking is:
    Dan identifies as African American.
    Dan is in stage C.
    the NYHA class of Dan is 3.
    the ejection fraction of Dan is 30.
    Dan has received standard neurohormonal antagonist therapy.
    combination expects answers [
        "the guideline recommends hydralazine plus isosorbide dinitrate with class 1 for Dan"]
        and unknowns [].

% NYHA class 2: the combination is not indicated, whatever is assumed.
scenario nyha_class_2 is:
    Dan identifies as African American.
    Dan is in stage C.
    the NYHA class of Dan is 2.
    the ejection fraction of Dan is 30.
    combination expects answers [].

query combination is:
    the guideline recommends hydralazine plus isosorbide dinitrate with which class for which patient.

query treatments is:
    the guideline recommends which treatment with which class for which patient.
